==German==

===Etymology 1===
From late {{etyl|gmh|de}} {{m|gmh|zimet}} (whence also modern German {{m|de|Zimmet}}), from {{etyl|gmh|de}} {{m|gmh|zinemīn}}, {{m|gmh|zinment}}, from {{etyl|la|de}}, from {{etyl|grc|de}}, from {{etyl|phn|de}}; for more, see "[[cinnamon]]".

====Noun====
{{de-noun|m|Zimts|gen2=Zimtes|-}}

# [[cinnamon]]

=====Synonyms=====
* (archaic) [[Zimmet]]

=====Related terms=====
* [[Zimtschnecke]]
* [[Zimtaldehyd]]
* [[Zimtbaum]]
* [[Zimtöl]]
* [[Zimtstange]]

===Etymology 2===
From the adjective {{m|de|zimt}}.

====Noun====
{{de-noun|n|Zimts|-}}

# the brownish colour of [[cinnamon]]

===Etymology 3===
From [[w:Rotwelsch|Rotwelsch]] {{m|de|Zimt||gold}}<!--, as in "Mach kein Gold", "Don't fake any gold"-->.

====Noun====
{{de-noun|m|Zimts|gen2=Zimtes|Zimte}}

# something worthless or dumb

=====Related terms=====
* [[Zimtzicke]]

